10\t  registry_id: v4-random-fixed-inject50-eval\n111\t  depends_on:\n112\t  - multiseed-vanilla\n113\t  results:\n114\t    inject0_baseline: 61.7% (vanilla seed=42)\n115\t    inject10: 68.1% (32/47, +6.4pp)\n116\t    inject25: 55.3% (26/47, -6.4pp)\n117\t    inject50: 57.4% (27/47, -4.3pp)\n118\t  notes: 'Train: v4-random-fixed-inject10, v4-random-fixed-inject25, v4-random-fixed-inject50.\n119\t    Eval: v4-random-fixed-inject10-eval, v4-random-fixed-inject25-eval, v4-random-fixed-inject50-eval.\n120\t    Random 10% positive effect contrasts with TaxEI 10% zero effect.'\n121\t- id: recovery-eval\n122\t  description: Recovery rate under injected errors (seed=42, 47 tasks, round-robin\n123\t    P1/P2/C1/C4)\n124\t  claim: C4,C5\n125\t  priority: 1\n126\t  status: done\n127\t  registry_id: v4-taxei-recovery-eval-r2\n128\t  depends_on:\n129\t  - multiseed-vanilla\n130\t  - multiseed-taxei\n131\t  - multiseed-random\n132\t  results:\n133\t    vanilla_recovery: 61.7%\n134\t    taxei_recovery: 59.6%\n135\t    random_recovery: 63.8%\n136\t    detection_rate: 0% (all methods)\n137\t    taxei_per_operator: C1=66.7%, C4=63.6%, P1=58.3%, P2=50.0%\n138\t  notes: 'All registry: v4-vanilla-recovery-eval, v4-taxei-recovery-eval, v4-taxei-recovery-eval-r2,\n139\t    v4-random-recovery-eval'\n140\t- id: recovery-paired-injection\n141\t  description: 'Recovery-paired error injection on ALFWorld: each injected error trajectory\n142\t    is immediately followed by the correct recovery demonstration (mimicking PALADIN''s\n143\t    recovery-pairing design). Compare TaxEI-RP vs TaxEI (unpaired) vs Vanilla to disentangle\n144\t    recovery-pairing from task-structure hypothesis.\n145\t\n146\t    '\n147\t  claim: C7\n148\t  priority: 1\n149\t  status: done\n150\t  depends_on:\n151\t  - multiseed-taxei\n152\t  - multiseed-vanilla\n153\t  results:\n154\t    seed42: 38.3%\n155\t    seed0: 46.8%\n156\t    seed1: 48.9%\n157\t    seed123: 57.4%\n158\t    mean_sd: 47.9% ± 7.8pp\n159\t    vs_taxei: -10.4pp (worse)\n160\t    vs_vanilla: -19.4pp (worse)\n161\t    detection_rate: 0% (all seeds)\n162\t    key_finding: Recovery pairing actively harms — not PALADIN's missing ingredient.\n163\t      Task structure confirmed as primary moderator (D043).\n164\t  notes: 'D043: Recovery-paired injection (14,437 samples = TaxEI 9,029 + recovery\n165\t    continuations 5,408) performs WORSE than unpaired TaxEI. Recovery demonstrations\n166\t    do not teach active recovery in embodied planning. Claim 7 definitively answered:\n167\t    No. s7 training in progress for 5th seed.'\n168\t  registry_id: v4-taxei-rp-s1\n169\t- id: webshop-replication\n170\t  description: 'CANCELLED (D040): Downgraded to Discussion section analysis. P1_StepOrderSwap\n171\t    incompatible with WebShop linear action space (search+click only). Taxonomy 4→3\n172\t    makes cross-env comparison inequivalent.'\n173\t  claim: C6\n174\t  priority: 1\n175\t  status: cancelled\n176\t  depends_on:\n177\t  - dose-response-random\n178\t  notes: 'D040: P1 produces illegal sequences in WebShop. 12-17 day workload, 35\n179\t    GPU-h (64% budget). Replaced by Discussion paragraph analyzing ALFWorld vs WebShop\n180\t    structural differences. GPU-h redirected to recovery eval multi-seed + TaxEI-RP\n181\t    seed 7.'\n182\t- id: 5-seed-extension\n183\t  description: Extend main conditions (Vanilla, TaxEI, Random full-scale) from 3 to\n184\t    5 seeds. Add seeds 1 and 7.\n185\t  claim: C1,C3\n186\t  priority: 1\n187\t  status: done\n188\t  depends_on:\n189\t  - multiseed-vanilla\n190\t  - multiseed-taxei\n191\t  - multiseed-random\n192\t  registry_id: v4-random-seed7\n193\t  results:\n194\t    vanilla_5seed: 67.3% ± 4.7pp (61.7/68.1/66.0/66.0/74.5)\n195\t    taxei_5seed: 58.3% ± 6.5pp (61.7/46.8/61.7/59.6/61.7)\n196\t    random_5seed: 58.3% ± 8.7pp (66.0/55.3/68.1/46.8/55.3)\n197\t    key_finding: TaxEI = Random = 58.3% = 137/235 identical means, taxonomy labels\n198\t      zero benefit\n199\t    vanilla_vs_injection_p: 0.039 (Welch, uncorrected), Bonferroni NS\n200\t    cohens_d_vanilla_taxei: 1.58\n201\t    cohens_d_vanilla_random: 1.28\n202\t    power_at_n5: 45.2%, need n=9 for 80%\n203\t  notes: 'D032: 5-seed data shows TaxEI=Random identical. Variance gradient reversed\n204\t    vs 3-seed: Vanilla(4.7) < TaxEI(6.5) < Random(8.7). Train: v4-vanilla-seed1/7,\n205\t    v4-taxei-seed1/7, v4-random-seed1/7. Eval: all *-eval variants.'\n206\t- id: recovery-eval-multiseed\n207\t  description: 'Recovery eval for seeds 0, 1, 7, 123 across Vanilla/TaxEI/Random.\n208\t    Validates per-operator patterns beyond seed=42. Need to retrain seed=0/123 checkpoints\n209\t    (cleaned from disk).\n210\t\n211\t    '\n212\t  claim: C4,C5\n213\t  priority: 1\n214\t  status: planned\n215\t  depends_on:\n216\t  - 5-seed-extension\n217\t  notes: 'Retrain seed=0/123 checkpoints (~6h), then run recovery eval on all 5 seeds\n218\t    per condition. Strengthens per-operator local/global split from exploratory to\n219\t    confirmatory. ~15 GPU-hours total.\n220\t\n221\t    '\n222\t- id: training-dynamics\n223\t  description: 'Per-sample loss analysis: clean vs injected loss trajectories across\n224\t    checkpoints. Forward pass on 6 checkpoints (3 TaxEI + 3 Random seeds).'\n225\t  claim: C3\n226\t  priority: 1\n227\t  status: done\n228\t  registry_id: v4-training-dynamics-forward-v2\n229\t  depends_on:\n230\t  - multiseed-taxei\n231\t  - multiseed-random\n232\t  results:\n233\t    training_loss_sd: 0.0004 (cross-seed, extremely stable)\n234\t    injected_vs_clean_loss: injected < clean (deeper memorization)\n235\t    key_finding: memorization-generalization dissociation — injected memorized better\n236\t      but eval worse\n237\t  notes: 'D027: Training loss stable SD=0.0004. D029: Forward pass v2 (trajectory-level)\n238\t    confirms injected samples memorized deeper. Per-operator loss inversely correlates\n239\t    with recovery harm. v1 had classification bug (turn-level), v2 fixed.'\n240\t- id: qualitative-failure-analysis\n241\t  description: 'Failure mode categorization across Vanilla/TaxEI/Random from eval\n242\t    logs. Key finding: TaxEI 2.2× loop_repetition rate.'\n243\t  claim: C1,C6\n244\t  priority: 1\n245\t  status: done\n246\t  registry_id: qualitative-failure-analysis\n247\t  depends_on:\n248\t  - 5-seed-extension\n249\t  results:\n250\t    taxei_loop_repetition_rate: ~2.2× Vanilla (unbalanced: 3-seed V/T 141 ep, 1-seed\n251\t      R 47 ep)\n252\t    vanilla_loop_repetition_rate: baseline reference\n253\t    random_loop_repetition_rate: ~similar to Vanilla\n254\t    key_finding: TaxEI loop_repetition ratio ~2.2× Vanilla stable across subsets.\n255\t      Absolute rates pending balanced 5-seed trajectory collection.\n256\t  notes: 'D026: Ratio (2.2×) directionally consistent but artifact metadata falsely\n257\t    claims \"balanced 235 episodes\". Actual: V=141, T=141, R=47. Clean eval trajectory\n258\t    collection needed for true 5-seed balance. Absolute percentages (34.8%/15.6%/12.8%)\n259\t    were extrapolated, not measured — do NOT use in paper without verification.'\n260\t- id: extended-stats\n261\t  description: Bootstrap CI, power analysis, effect size, Bayesian analysis for 5-seed\n262\t    data.\n263\t  claim: C1,C3\n264\t  priority: 1\n265\t  status: done\n266\t  depends_on:\n267\t  - 5-seed-extension\n268\t  results:\n269\t    bootstrap_ci_95: '[+3.4, +15.8] pp (Vanilla - injection pooled)'\n270\t    paired_t_p: 0.073 (marginal)\n271\t    welch_t_p: 0.039 (uncorrected), Bonferroni NS\n272\t    bayes_factor: 0.68 (inconclusive)\n273\t    power_at_n5: 45.2%\n274\t    n_needed_80pct_power: 9\n275\t    cohens_d_vanilla_taxei: 1.58\n276\t    cohens_d_vanilla_random: 1.28\n277\t    taxei_vs_random_p: 1.000 (identical means)\n278\t  notes: 'D030-D032: Complete 5-seed statistical analysis. Large effect size but underpowered.\n279\t    Bayesian inconclusive. Bootstrap significant. Variance test: Levene p=0.45 (NS).'\n280\t- id: dose-response-5seed\n281\t  description: 'Extend all dose-response to 5 seeds: 10% (from 1→5), 25%/50% (from\n282\t    3→5). Both TaxEI and Random.'\n283\t  claim: C3\n284\t  priority: 1\n285\t  status: done\n286\t  depends_on:\n287\t  - 5-seed-extension\n288\t  registry_id: v4-random-fixed-inject50-s7\n289\t  results:\n290\t    taxei_10pct: 61.3% ± 8.2pp (61.7/70.2/55.3/51.1/68.1)\n291\t    random_10pct: 63.8% ± 5.4pp (68.1/66.0/55.3/68.1/61.7)\n292\t    taxei_25pct: 52.7% ± 7.6pp (48.9/46.8/46.8/63.8/57.4)\n293\t    random_25pct: 60.0% ± 8.0pp (55.3/61.7/51.1/72.3/59.6)\n294\t    taxei_50pct: 57.4% ± 9.5pp (51.1/70.2/46.8/63.8/55.3)\n295\t    random_50pct: 58.3% ± 11.7pp (57.4/46.8/70.2/70.2/46.8)\n296\t    key_finding: 'Inverted-U taxonomy penalty: 10% (-2.5pp) → 25% (-7.3pp peak) →\n297\t      50% (-0.9pp) → Full (0pp). No safe dose. Universal training lottery at all doses.'\n298\t  notes: 'D034/D035/D036/D038: Complete 5-seed dose-response. 10% overturned D017\n299\t    zero-harm. 25% overturned D023 deterministic-harm. 50% confirms rebound. Taxonomy\n300\t    penalty peaks at 25% and fades. ~24 GPU-hours total.'\n301\t- id: scale-ablation\n302\t  description: Scale to 25K-50K trajectories to match PALADIN's data scale\n303\t  claim: C6\n304\t  priority: 2\n305\t  status: planned\n306\t  depends_on:\n307\t  - dose-response-random\n308\t  notes: 'Tests whether TaxEI''s failure is due to insufficient data scale. Need additional\n309\t    GPT-5.2 trajectory collection (~$30-50).\n310\t\n311\t    '\n312\t- id: recovery-prompting\n313\t  description: In-context recovery examples (few-shot) to isolate training signal\n314\t    vs knowledge\n315\t  claim: C6\n316\t  priority: 3\n317\t  status: planned\n318\t  depends_on:\n319\t  - recovery-eval\n320\t- id: per-operator-deepdive\n321\t  description: Multi-seed recovery eval to validate per-operator patterns (esp. C4\n322\t    +9.1pp)\n323\t  claim: C4\n324\t  priority: 3\n325\t  status: planned\n326\t  depends_on:\n327\t  - recovery-eval\n328\t- id: llama-cross-model\n329\t  description: 'LLaMA-3.1-8B cross-model replication: 3-seed Vanilla/TaxEI/Random\n330\t    on ALFWorld. Tests whether negative result generalizes beyond Qwen3-8B.'\n331\t  claim: C1,C2,C6\n332\t  priority: 1\n333\t  status: planned\n334\t  depends_on:\n335\t  - multiseed-vanilla\n336\t  - multiseed-taxei\n337\t  - multiseed-random\n338\t  notes: 'D042/D045: 3-seed V/T/R (s42/s0/s123). Same training data, same LoRA config\n339\t    (rank=16, α=32), same eval. LLaMA 3.1-8B is the latest non-MoE LLaMA at 8B scale.\n340\t    s42 training in progress (GPU 0-2). s0/s123 after s42 eval. ~16 GPU-h total.\n341\t    Model: Meta-Llama-3.1-8B-Instruct at /root/autodl-tmp/models/Meta-Llama-3.1-8B-Instruct/'\n342\t- id: scale-up-data\n343\t  description: 'Scale trajectory collection from 500→2500 successful trajectories\n344\t    via GPT-5.2. Tests whether TaxEI failure is due to insufficient data scale (PALADIN\n345\t    uses 50K+).'\n346\t  claim: C6\n347\t  priority: 1\n348\t  status: planned\n349\t  depends_on:\n350\t  - data-collection\n351\t  notes: 'Scope expansion (D042). GATE: verify ALFWorld task pool ≥3500 games before\n352\t    API spend. ~$47 API cost. Reduced scope: 3-seed V+T only (~17h GPU with DDP),\n353\t    not full 5-seed×3 (~44h). Phased: collect 1000 first, check trend, then decide\n354\t    2500. CAVEAT: ALFWorld only has ~134 unique tasks, so 2500 trajectories ≈ 19/task\n355\t    — still far below PALADIN task diversity. Frame as: within ALFWorld diversity ceiling,\n356\t    scale is not the bottleneck.'\n357\t  notes: Merged into recovery-eval-multiseed for long paper\n358\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4482c8d4-fab8-4afb-aeb3-2474cc94062c","uuid":"be4d4592-8b89-4ef2-86f9-0485f2b305ad","timestamp":"2026-05-16T15:53:39.469Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0514_2/projects/tax_error_inject_agent/experiment_plan.yaml","content":"experiments:\n- id: baseline\n  description: Qwen3-8B zero-shot ReAct baseline on ALFWorld (47 tasks)\n  claim: context\n  priority: 0\n  status: done\n  registry_id: vanilla-react-baseline\n  depends_on: []\n  results:\n    accuracy: 42.6% (20/47)\n- id: data-collection\n  description: GPT-5.2 trajectory collection for SFT training data\n  claim: prerequisite\n  priority: 0\n  status: done\n  registry_id: traj_collect_500\n  depends_on: []\n  results:\n    success_rate: 70.2% (501/714)\n    cost: $8.86\n- id: v3-pilot\n  description: 'v3 format-aligned pilot: vanilla/TaxEI/random single-seed eval'\n  claim: supplement\n  priority: 0\n  status: done\n  registry_id: v3-vanilla-eval\n  depends_on:\n  - data-collection\n  results:\n    vanilla: 74.5%\n    taxei: 66.0%\n    random: 51.1%\n  notes: 'Superseded by v4. All registry: mini-vanilla-sft-v3, mini-taxei-sft-v3,\n    mini-random-sft-v3, v3-vanilla-eval, v3-taxei-eval, v3-random-eval'\n- id: multiseed-vanilla\n  description: Vanilla SFT 3-seed verification (clean data only, 4,358 samples)\n  claim: C1\n  priority: 1\n  status: done\n  registry_id: v4-vanilla-eval-r3\n  depends_on:\n  - data-collection\n  results:\n    seed42: 61.7%\n    seed0: 68.1%\n    seed123: 66.0%\n    mean_sd: 65.3% ± 3.3pp\n  notes: 'Train: mini-vanilla-sft-v4, v4-vanilla-seed0, v4-vanilla-seed123. Eval:\n    v4-vanilla-eval-r3, v4-vanilla-seed0-eval, v4-vanilla-seed123-eval'\n- id: multiseed-taxei\n  description: TaxEI SFT 3-seed verification (clean + taxonomy-tagged injections,\n    9,029 samples)\n  claim: C1,C2,C3\n  priority: 1\n  status: done\n  registry_id: v4-taxei-eval\n  depends_on:\n  - data-collection\n  results:\n    seed42: 61.7%\n    seed0: 46.8%\n    seed123: 61.7%\n    mean_sd: 56.7% ± 8.6pp\n    vs_vanilla_paired_t_p: 0.32 (NS)\n    vs_vanilla_pooled_p: 0.054 (NS at α=0.05)\n  notes: 'Train: v4-taxei-sft-r2, v4-taxei-seed0, v4-taxei-seed123. Eval: v4-taxei-eval,\n    v4-taxei-seed0-eval, v4-taxei-seed123-eval'\n- id: multiseed-random\n  description: Random SFT 3-seed verification (clean + unlabeled injections, 9,029\n    samples)\n  claim: C2,C3\n  priority: 1\n  status: done\n  registry_id: v4-random-eval\n  depends_on:\n  - data-collection\n  results:\n    seed42: 66.0%\n    seed0: 55.3%\n    seed123: 68.1%\n    mean_sd: 63.1% ± 7.0pp\n    vs_taxei_paired_t_p: 0.034 (suggestive, df=2)\n    vs_taxei_pooled_p: 0.170 (NS)\n  notes: 'Train: v4-random-sft-r2, v4-random-seed0, v4-random-seed123. Eval: v4-random-eval,\n    v4-random-seed0-eval, v4-random-seed123-eval'\n- id: dose-response-taxei\n  description: TaxEI dose-response curve (10%/25%/50% injection, fixed 4,358 total,\n    seed=42)\n  claim: C3\n  priority: 1\n  status: done\n  registry_id: v4-taxei-fixed-inject50-eval\n  depends_on:\n  - multiseed-vanilla\n  results:\n    inject0_baseline: 61.7% (vanilla seed=42)\n    inject10: 61.7% (0pp)\n    inject25: 48.9% (-12.8pp)\n    inject50: 51.1% (-10.6pp)\n    pattern: 'threshold-plateau: 10% harmless, 25% catastrophic collapse, 50% no further\n      worsening'\n  notes: 'Train: v4-taxei-fixed-inject10, v4-taxei-fixed-inject25-r2, v4-taxei-fixed-inject50.\n    Eval: v4-taxei-fixed-inject10-eval, v4-taxei-fixed-inject25-eval, v4-taxei-fixed-inject50-eval'\n- id: dose-response-random\n  description: Random dose-response curve (10%/25%/50% injection, fixed 4,358 total,\n    seed=42)\n  claim: C3\n  priority: 1\n  status: done\n  registry_id: v4-random-fixed-inject50-eval\n  depends_on:\n  - multiseed-vanilla\n  results:\n    inject0_baseline: 61.7% (vanilla seed=42)\n    inject10: 68.1% (32/47, +6.4pp)\n    inject25: 55.3% (26/47, -6.4pp)\n    inject50: 57.4% (27/47, -4.3pp)\n  notes: 'Train: v4-random-fixed-inject10, v4-random-fixed-inject25, v4-random-fixed-inject50.\n    Eval: v4-random-fixed-inject10-eval, v4-random-fixed-inject25-eval, v4-random-fixed-inject50-eval.\n    Random 10% positive effect contrasts with TaxEI 10% zero effect.'\n- id: recovery-eval\n  description: Recovery rate under injected errors (seed=42, 47 tasks, round-robin\n    P1/P2/C1/C4)\n  claim: C4,C5\n  priority: 1\n  status: done\n  registry_id: v4-taxei-recovery-eval-r2\n  depends_on:\n  - multiseed-vanilla\n  - multiseed-taxei\n  - multiseed-random\n  results:\n    vanilla_recovery: 61.7%\n    taxei_recovery: 59.6%\n    random_recovery: 63.8%\n    detection_rate: 0% (all methods)\n    taxei_per_operator: C1=66.7%, C4=63.6%, P1=58.3%, P2=50.0%\n  notes: 'All registry: v4-vanilla-recovery-eval, v4-taxei-recovery-eval, v4-taxei-recovery-eval-r2,\n    v4-random-recovery-eval'\n- id: recovery-paired-injection\n  description: 'Recovery-paired error injection on ALFWorld: each injected error trajectory\n    is immediately followed by the correct recovery demonstration (mimicking PALADIN''s\n    recovery-pairing design). Compare TaxEI-RP vs TaxEI (unpaired) vs Vanilla to disentangle\n    recovery-pairing from task-structure hypothesis.\n\n    '\n  claim: C7\n  priority: 1\n  status: done\n  depends_on:\n  - multiseed-taxei\n  - multiseed-vanilla\n  results:\n    seed42: 38.3%\n    seed0: 46.8%\n    seed1: 48.9%\n    seed123: 57.4%\n    mean_sd: 47.9% ± 7.8pp\n    vs_taxei: -10.4pp (worse)\n    vs_vanilla: -19.4pp (worse)\n    detection_rate: 0% (all seeds)\n    key_finding: Recovery pairing actively harms — not PALADIN's missing ingredient.\n      Task structure confirmed as primary moderator (D043).\n  notes: 'D043: Recovery-paired injection (14,437 samples = TaxEI 9,029 + recovery\n    continuations 5,408) performs WORSE than unpaired TaxEI. Recovery demonstrations\n    do not teach active recovery in embodied planning. Claim 7 definitively answered:\n    No. s7 training in progress for 5th seed.'\n  registry_id: v4-taxei-rp-s1\n- id: webshop-replication\n  description: 'CANCELLED (D040): Downgraded to Discussion section analysis. P1_StepOrderSwap\n    incompatible with WebShop linear action space (search+click only). Taxonomy 4→3\n    makes cross-env comparison inequivalent.'\n  claim: C6\n  priority: 1\n  status: cancelled\n  depends_on:\n  - dose-response-random\n  notes: 'D040: P1 produces illegal sequences in WebShop. 12-17 day workload, 35\n    GPU-h (64% budget). Replaced by Discussion paragraph analyzing ALFWorld vs WebShop\n    structural differences. GPU-h redirected to recovery eval multi-seed + TaxEI-RP\n    seed 7.'\n- id: 5-seed-extension\n  description: Extend main conditions (Vanilla, TaxEI, Random full-scale) from 3 to\n    5 seeds. Add seeds 1 and 7.\n  claim: C1,C3\n  priority: 1\n  status: done\n  depends_on:\n  - multiseed-vanilla\n  - multiseed-taxei\n  - multiseed-random\n  registry_id: v4-random-seed7\n  results:\n    vanilla_5seed: 67.3% ± 4.7pp (61.7/68.1/66.0/66.0/74.5)\n    taxei_5seed: 58.3% ± 6.5pp (61.7/46.8/61.7/59.6/61.7)\n    random_5seed: 58.3% ± 8.7pp (66.0/55.3/68.1/46.8/55.3)\n    key_finding: TaxEI = Random = 58.3% = 137/235 identical means, taxonomy labels\n      zero benefit\n    vanilla_vs_injection_p: 0.039 (Welch, uncorrected), Bonferroni NS\n    cohens_d_vanilla_taxei: 1.58\n    cohens_d_vanilla_random: 1.28\n    power_at_n5: 45.2%, need n=9 for 80%\n  notes: 'D032: 5-seed data shows TaxEI=Random identical. Variance gradient reversed\n    vs 3-seed: Vanilla(4.7) < TaxEI(6.5) < Random(8.7). Train: v4-vanilla-seed1/7,\n    v4-taxei-seed1/7, v4-random-seed1/7. Eval: all *-eval variants.'\n- id: recovery-eval-multiseed\n  description: 'Recovery eval for seeds 0, 1, 7, 123 across Vanilla/TaxEI/Random.\n    Validates per-operator patterns beyond seed=42. Need to retrain seed=0/123 checkpoints\n    (cleaned from disk).\n\n    '\n  claim: C4,C5\n  priority: 1\n  status: planned\n  depends_on:\n  - 5-seed-extension\n  notes: 'Retrain seed=0/123 checkpoints (~6h), then run recovery eval on all 5 seeds\n    per condition. Strengthens per-operator local/global split from exploratory to\n    confirmatory. ~15 GPU-hours total.\n\n    '\n- id: training-dynamics\n  description: 'Per-sample loss analysis: clean vs injected loss trajectories across\n    checkpoints. Forward pass on 6 checkpoints (3 TaxEI + 3 Random seeds).'\n  claim: C3\n  priority: 1\n  status: done\n  registry_id: v4-training-dynamics-forward-v2\n  depends_on:\n  - multiseed-taxei\n  - multiseed-random\n  results:\n    training_loss_sd: 0.0004 (cross-seed, extremely stable)\n    injected_vs_clean_loss: injected < clean (deeper memorization)\n    key_finding: memorization-generalization dissociation — injected memorized better\n      but eval worse\n  notes: 'D027: Training loss stable SD=0.0004. D029: Forward pass v2 (trajectory-level)\n    confirms injected samples memorized deeper. Per-operator loss inversely correlates\n    with recovery harm. v1 had classification bug (turn-level), v2 fixed.'\n- id: qualitative-failure-analysis\n  description: 'Failure mode categorization across Vanilla/TaxEI/Random from eval\n    logs. Key finding: TaxEI 2.2× loop_repetition rate.'\n  claim: C1,C6\n  priority: 1\n  status: done\n  registry_id: qualitative-failure-analysis\n  depends_on:\n  - 5-seed-extension\n  results:\n    taxei_loop_repetition_rate: ~2.2× Vanilla (unbalanced: 3-seed V/T 141 ep, 1-seed\n      R 47 ep)\n    vanilla_loop_repetition_rate: baseline reference\n    random_loop_repetition_rate: ~similar to Vanilla\n    key_finding: TaxEI loop_repetition ratio ~2.2× Vanilla stable across subsets.\n      Absolute rates pending balanced 5-seed trajectory collection.\n  notes: 'D026: Ratio (2.2×) directionally consistent but artifact metadata falsely\n    claims \"balanced 235 episodes\". Actual: V=141, T=141, R=47. Clean eval trajectory\n    collection needed for true 5-seed balance. Absolute percentages (34.8%/15.6%/12.8%)\n    were extrapolated, not measured — do NOT use in paper without verification.'\n- id: extended-stats\n  description: Bootstrap CI, power analysis, effect size, Bayesian analysis for 5-seed\n    data.\n  claim: C1,C3\n  priority: 1\n  status: done\n  depends_on:\n  - 5-seed-extension\n  results:\n    bootstrap_ci_95: '[+3.4, +15.8] pp (Vanilla - injection pooled)'\n    paired_t_p: 0.073 (marginal)\n    welch_t_p: 0.039 (uncorrected), Bonferroni NS\n    bayes_factor: 0.68 (inconclusive)\n    power_at_n5: 45.2%\n    n_needed_80pct_power: 9\n    cohens_d_vanilla_taxei: 1.58\n    cohens_d_vanilla_random: 1.28\n    taxei_vs_random_p: 1.000 (identical means)\n  notes: 'D030-D032: Complete 5-seed statistical analysis. Large effect size but underpowered.\n    Bayesian inconclusive. Bootstrap significant. Variance test: Levene p=0.45 (NS).'\n- id: dose-response-5seed\n  description: 'Extend all dose-response to 5 seeds: 10% (from 1→5), 25%/50% (from\n    3→5). Both TaxEI and Random.'\n  claim: C3\n  priority: 1\n  status: done\n  depends_on:\n  - 5-seed-extension\n  registry_id: v4-random-fixed-inject50-s7\n  results:\n    taxei_10pct: 61.3% ± 8.2pp (61.7/70.2/55.3/51.1/68.1)\n    random_10pct: 63.8% ± 5.4pp (68.1/66.0/55.3/68.1/61.7)\n    taxei_25pct: 52.7% ± 7.6pp (48.9/46.8/46.8/63.8/57.4)\n    random_25pct: 60.0% ± 8.0pp (55.3/61.7/51.1/72.3/59.6)\n    taxei_50pct: 57.4% ± 9.5pp (51.1/70.2/46.8/63.8/55.3)\n    random_50pct: 58.3% ± 11.7pp (57.4/46.8/70.2/70.2/46.8)\n    key_finding: 'Inverted-U taxonomy penalty: 10% (-2.5pp) → 25% (-7.3pp peak) →\n      50% (-0.9pp) → Full (0pp). No safe dose. Universal training lottery at all doses.'\n  notes: 'D034/D035/D036/D038: Complete 5-seed dose-response. 10% overturned D017\n    zero-harm. 25% overturned D023 deterministic-harm. 50% confirms rebound. Taxonomy\n    penalty peaks at 25% and fades. ~24 GPU-hours total.'\n- id: scale-ablation\n  description: Scale to 25K-50K trajectories to match PALADIN's data scale\n  claim: C6\n  priority: 2\n  status: planned\n  depends_on:\n  - dose-response-random\n  notes: 'Tests whether TaxEI''s failure is due to insufficient data scale. Need additional\n    GPT-5.2 trajectory collection (~$30-50).\n\n    '\n- id: recovery-prompting\n  description: In-context recovery examples (few-shot) to isolate training signal\n    vs knowledge\n  claim: C6\n  priority: 3\n  status: planned\n  depends_on:\n  - recovery-eval\n- id: per-operator-deepdive\n  description: Multi-seed recovery eval to validate per-operator patterns (esp. C4\n    +9.1pp)\n  claim: C4\n  priority: 3\n  status: planned\n  depends_on:\n  - recovery-eval\n- id: llama-cross-model\n  description: 'LLaMA-3.1-8B cross-model replication: 3-seed Vanilla/TaxEI/Random\n    on ALFWorld. Tests whether negative result generalizes beyond Qwen3-8B.'\n  claim: C1,C2,C6\n  priority: 1\n  status: planned\n  depends_on:\n  - multiseed-vanilla\n  - multiseed-taxei\n  - multiseed-random\n  notes: 'D042/D045: 3-seed V/T/R (s42/s0/s123). Same training data, same LoRA config\n    (rank=16, α=32), same eval. LLaMA 3.1-8B is the latest non-MoE LLaMA at 8B scale.\n    s42 training in progress (GPU 0-2). s0/s123 after s42 eval. ~16 GPU-h total.\n    Model: Meta-Llama-3.1-8B-Instruct at /root/autodl-tmp/models/Meta-Llama-3.1-8B-Instruct/'\n- id: scale-up-data\n  description: 'Scale trajectory collection from 500→2500 successful trajectories\n    via GPT-5.2. Tests whether TaxEI failure is due to insufficient data scale (PALADIN\n    uses 50K+).'\n  claim: C6\n  priority: 1\n  status: planned\n  depends_on:\n  - data-collection\n  notes: 'Scope expansion (D042). GATE: verify ALFWorld task pool ≥3500 games before\n    API spend. ~$47 API cost. Reduced scope: 3-seed V+T only (~17h GPU with DDP),\n    not full 5-seed×3 (~44h). Phased: collect 1000 first, check trend, then decide\n    2500. CAVEAT: ALFWorld only has ~134 unique tasks, so 2500 trajectories ≈ 19/task\n    — still far below PALADIN task diversity. Frame as: within ALFWorld diversity ceiling,\n    scale is not the bottleneck.'\n  notes: Merged into recovery-eval-multiseed for long paper\n","numLines":358,"startLine":1,"totalLines":358}}}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_012n4gc39Ca72w6DZuDac4sB","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I have all the experiment plan data. Let me identify the \"planned\" experiments:\n\n1. **recovery-eval-multiseed** (id: recovery-eval-multiseed) - Recovery eval for seeds 0, 1, 7, 123 across Vanilla/TaxEI/Random. Status: planned.\n2. **scale-ablation** (id: scale-ablation) - Scale to 25K-50K trajectories. Priority 2, status: planned.\n3. **recovery-prompting** (id: recovery-prompting) - In-context recovery examples (few-shot). Priority 3, status: planned.\n\n\n4. **per-operator-deepdive** (id: per-operator-deepdive) - Multi-seed recovery eval to validate per-operator patterns. Priority 3, status: planned.\n5. **llama-cross-model** (id: llama-cross-model) - LLaMA-3.1-8B cross-model replication marked as planned in the experiment plan, though the registry data suggests it's actually completed.\n6. **scale-up-data** (id: scale-up-data) - Scale trajectory collection from 500→2500. Status: planned.\n\nI'm noticing a discrepancy with the llama-cross-model experiment—the plan shows it as planned but the registry data indicates it's already done.\n\nNow I'm thinking through what the worst-case scenario would look like for these planned experiments. For recovery-eval-multiseed, the per-operator patterns wouldn't hold up across different seeds, and the C4 advantage would disappear into noise. The recovery-resilience connection would survive but get dismissed as trivial. For scale-ablation, I'm working through what happens when we push to 25K tokens. The cross-model findings hold up directionally, but reviewers will likely treat them as anecdotal rather than conclusive. For the scale-up experiments, even pushing to 5× more trajectories still shows TaxEI degrading performance, though critics will argue ALFWorld's 134 tasks don't match PALADIN's diversity. Now I'm calibrating the worst-case metrics into the YAML output with specific ranges for the main effect sizes and failure modes.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":11060,"cache_read_input_tokens":54223,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":11060},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4482c8d4-fab8-4afb-aeb3-2474cc94062c","uuid":"a7e9d0dc-8fae-401e-b75a-edeb1e9bc595"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_012n4gc39Ca72w6DZuDac4sB","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Now I have all the planned experiments. Let me produce the detailed worst-tier predictions.\n\n```yaml\ntier: worst\nnarrative_guidance: >\n  Reviewers读到paper后的反应：'error injection hurts embodied planning'被视为trivially expected negative result，\n  3-seed LLaMA被dismisses为anecdotal，Bonferroni NS让所有statistical claims失去说服力。\n  Recovery=Resilience finding被认为'obviously true for any model without explicit error signals'。\n  需要彻底reframe——从domain-transfer negative result转为(A)Training Lottery methodological warning、\n  (B)Resilience-vs-Recovery paradigm challenge、或(C)Structured vs Unstructured augmentation stability principle。\n  选择取决于reviewer主要reject reason：若'obvious negative result'选A/C，若'not novel enough'选B。\n\nimagined_experiments:\n  - name: \"Recovery Eval Multi-Seed (5-seed × 3 conditions)\"\n    plan_id: \"recovery-eval-multiseed\"\n    description: >\n      Recovery eval扩展到全部5 seeds × 3 conditions (Vanilla/TaxEI/Random)，验证per-operator\n      local/global split是否跨seed可复现。需retrain seed=0/123 checkpoints。\n    expected_results:\n      vanilla_recovery_mean: 0.653\n      vanilla_recovery_sd_pp: 4.8\n      taxei_recovery_mean: 0.572\n      taxei_recovery_sd_pp: 7.2\n      random_recovery_mean: 0.581\n      random_recovery_sd_pp: 8.1\n      detection_rate_all: 0.0\n      per_operator_C4_taxei_advantage_pp: 2.3\n      per_operator_C4_pvalue: 0.41\n      per_operator_C1_taxei_disadvantage_pp: -4.8\n      per_operator_P2_taxei_disadvantage_pp: -3.1\n      per_operator_pattern_replicates: false\n      recovery_vs_clean_rate_delta_pp: 1.4\n    result_rationale: >\n      在worst档位下，seed=42的C4 +9.1pp优势是N=11的随机波动——扩展到5-seed后平均只剩+2.3pp，\n      Fisher exact NS (p=0.41)。Per-operator local/global split从\"suggestive pattern\"降级为\n      \"within noise\"。然而recovery≈resilience的核心发现(delta<2pp)仍然稳健——5-seed数据确认\n      所有condition的recovery rate与clean rate匹配在2pp以内。但reviewer会说\"当然model不detect——\n      你没给它explicit error signal，这是trivially expected\"。Detection=0%在没有explicit error\n      marker的eval中是obvious的。整个recovery eval被读作confirmatory of the obvious。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Table: 5-Seed Recovery Rate (Injected Eval, 47 tasks)\"\n        data:\n          columns: [Condition, s42, s0, s1, s7, s123, \"Mean±SD\"]\n          rows:\n            - [Vanilla, \"61.7%\", \"68.1%\", \"66.0%\", \"74.5%\", \"61.7%\", \"66.4±5.1%\"]\n            - [TaxEI, \"59.6%\", \"46.8%\", \"61.7%\", \"61.7%\", \"55.3%\", \"57.0±6.2%\"]\n            - [Random, \"63.8%\", \"55.3%\", \"51.1%\", \"55.3%\", \"66.0%\", \"58.3±6.4%\"]\n      - title: \"Table: Per-Operator Recovery Advantage (TaxEI - Vanilla, 5-seed mean)\"\n        data:\n          columns: [Operator, \"TaxEI mean\", \"Vanilla mean\", \"Δpp\", \"Fisher p\"]\n          rows:\n            - [C4_observation_masking, \"58.2%\", \"55.9%\", \"+2.3\", \"0.41\"]\n            - [P1_step_order_swap, \"56.2%\", \"58.3%\", \"-2.1\", \"0.68\"]\n            - [C1_context_truncation, \"60.8%\", \"65.6%\", \"-4.8\", \"0.33\"]\n            - [P2_sub_goal_deletion, \"52.9%\", \"56.0%\", \"-3.1\", \"0.52\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Heatmap: per-operator × per-seed recovery rate差异，颜色编码TaxEI-Vanilla gap。显示高seed-to-seed variability，无一致的operator-level pattern\"\n      - \"Bar plot: recovery rate vs clean eval rate overlay (5-seed mean)，误差棒重叠，视觉确认recovery≈resilience\"\n    analysis: >\n      5-seed recovery data确认两个finding：(1) Recovery=Resilience稳健（所有condition delta<2pp），\n      (2) Per-operator local/global split不可复现（C4 advantage从+9.1pp缩到+2.3pp，NS）。\n      Reviewer反应：\"Recovery≈resilience is obvious when there's no explicit error signal in the\n      observation space. You didn't test whether models could recover if TOLD about the error.\n      The per-operator analysis is just noise at N=11-12.\" 这削弱了Claim 4的novelty——finding成立\n      但被认为trivially expected。对reframe的贡献：支撑angle (B) Resilience-vs-Recovery，但需要\n      更强的framing来argue为什么community应该care about confirming the obvious。\n\n  - name: \"LLaMA-3.1-8B Cross-Model Replication (3-seed)\"\n    plan_id: \"llama-cross-model\"\n    description: >\n      LLaMA-3.1-8B-Instruct上复制Vanilla/TaxEI/Random × 3 seeds (s42/s0/s123)。\n      验证TaxEI instability是否为cross-architecture通用现象。\n    expected_results:\n      llama_vanilla_mean: 0.731\n      llama_vanilla_sd_pp: 2.5\n      llama_taxei_mean: 0.695\n      llama_taxei_sd_pp: 8.6\n      llama_random_mean: 0.766\n      llama_random_sd_pp: 2.1\n      taxei_sd_ratio_vs_random: 4.1\n      catastrophic_seed_count: 1\n      catastrophic_seed_fraction: 0.33\n      catastrophic_seed_drop_pp: -13.5\n      llama_taxei_vs_vanilla_gap_pp: -3.6\n      llama_random_vs_vanilla_gap_pp: 3.5\n      detection_rate_llama: 0.255\n    result_rationale: >\n      Worst档下，LLaMA 3-seed结果本身是real的（SD ratio=4.1x，1/3 catastrophic），但reviewer\n      dismiss方式是：\"3 seeds with 1 outlier proves nothing. Your 'catastrophic seed' at 59.6%\n      could be a single unlucky initialization. LLaMA also shows higher detection rate (25.5%\n      vs Qwen 0%) which you haven't adequately explained — maybe LLaMA IS learning something\n      from the injection that Qwen isn't, undermining your 'structured injection is universally\n      harmful' claim.\" 额外问题：LLaMA的Random=76.6% > Vanilla=73.1%与Qwen的Random=58.3% < \n      Vanilla=67.3%方向相反，reviewer认为这证明effect是model-specific而非injection-type-specific。\n      Cross-model \"same direction\"的claim被challenge——direction only holds for TaxEI≤Vanilla，\n      不hold for Random vs Vanilla。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Table: LLaMA-3.1-8B Recovery Rate (Injected Eval, 47 tasks, 3-seed)\"\n        data:\n          columns: [Condition, s42, s0, s123, \"Mean±SD\"]\n          rows:\n            - [Vanilla, \"74.5%\", \"74.5%\", \"70.2%\", \"73.1±2.5%\"]\n            - [TaxEI, \"74.5%\", \"74.5%\", \"59.6%\", \"69.5±8.6%\"]\n            - [Random, \"76.6%\", \"74.5%\", \"78.7%\", \"76.6±2.1%\"]\n      - title: \"Table: Cross-Model Comparison Summary\"\n        data:\n          columns: [Metric, Qwen3-8B, LLaMA-3.1-8B, \"Cross-model consistent?\"]\n          rows:\n            - [\"TaxEI vs Vanilla Δ\", \"-9.0pp\", \"-3.6pp\", \"Direction yes, magnitude no\"]\n            - [\"Random vs Vanilla Δ\", \"-9.0pp\", \"+3.5pp\", \"INCONSISTENT\"]\n            - [\"TaxEI SD / Random SD\", \"0.75×\", \"4.1×\", \"INCONSISTENT\"]\n            - [\"Catastrophic seed fraction\", \"1/5=20%\", \"1/3=33%\", \"Both present\"]\n            - [\"Detection rate\", \"0%\", \"25.5%\", \"INCONSISTENT\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Paired dot plot: Qwen vs LLaMA per-condition means with error bars，标注方向一致性。Random在两个model上方向相反（箭头标红）\"\n      - \"Variance ratio comparison: TaxEI_SD/Random_SD for both models，但Qwen是<1 (0.75)，LLaMA是>1 (4.1)——方向也相反\"\n    analysis: >\n      Cross-model validation在worst档下被reviewer拆解为self-contradictory evidence。核心问题：\n      (1) Random injection在Qwen上harmful、在LLaMA上beneficial——证明injection effect是model-specific；\n      (2) Qwen的TaxEI SD < Random SD，LLaMA的TaxEI SD > Random SD——variance pattern也model-specific；\n      (3) LLaMA有25.5% detection rate而Qwen有0%——说明'no error awareness'不是universal的。\n      唯一cross-model consistent的finding是'TaxEI has at least one catastrophic seed'，但\n      这在3-seed下就是\"one bad run\"。Reviewer结论：\"Your cross-model results actually WEAKEN\n      your main claims rather than strengthening them. The only thing that replicates is that\n      sometimes training is bad, which is obvious.\" 对reframe意义：强力支撑angle (A) Training\n      Lottery——因为within-condition variance > between-condition variance在两个model上都成立。\n\n  - name: \"Scale-Up Data Collection (500→2500 trajectories)\"\n    plan_id: \"scale-up-data\"\n    description: >\n      将训练数据从501 successful trajectories扩展到2500，测试TaxEI failure是否因数据规模不足。\n      ALFWorld仅134 unique tasks，2500 trajectories ≈ 19/task。3-seed V+T only。\n    expected_results:\n      trajectories_collected: 2500\n      collection_cost_usd: 47\n      unique_tasks_coverage: 134\n      trajectories_per_task_mean: 18.7\n      vanilla_2500_mean_3seed: 0.702\n      vanilla_2500_sd_pp: 3.8\n      taxei_2500_mean_3seed: 0.645\n      taxei_2500_sd_pp: 5.9\n      taxei_vs_vanilla_gap_2500_pp: -5.7\n      gap_reduction_vs_500_pp: 3.3\n      still_harmful: true\n      paladin_scale_fraction: 0.05\n    result_rationale: >\n      在worst档下，scale-up results会shows TaxEI harm从-9pp缩小到-5.7pp——证明scale部分mitigate，\n      但reviewer的response是：\"(1) You only went to 2500 out of PALADIN's 50K+ — that's 5%.\n      Maybe at 50K it would work. (2) ALFWorld has only 134 unique tasks, so 2500 trajectories\n      is just 19× repetition of the same 134 tasks — this doesn't test diversity scaling,\n      only repetition scaling. (3) The gap narrowed from 9pp to 5.7pp, which is exactly\n      what you'd expect from any data augmentation with more data — this doesn't tell us\n      anything about error injection specifically vs just having more varied data.\" 更致命的是：\n      5-seed下Bonferroni仍然NS，减少到3-seed (n=3 × 47 tasks) 下power更差。Scale experiment\n      既没有definitively证明\"scale fixes it\"也没有证明\"scale can't fix it\"——inconclusive，\n      浪费了$47 + 17h GPU但没有给paper增加convincing evidence。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Table: Scale Ablation Results (3-seed)\"\n        data:\n          columns: [Scale, \"Vanilla Mean±SD\", \"TaxEI Mean±SD\", \"Δpp\", \"Welch t p\"]\n          rows:\n            - [\"501 traj (current)\", \"67.3±4.7%\", \"58.3±6.5%\", \"-9.0\", \"0.039*\"]\n            - [\"2500 traj (5×)\", \"70.2±3.8%\", \"64.5±5.9%\", \"-5.7\", \"0.18 (NS)\"]\n          note: \"* uncorrected; Bonferroni NS at both scales\"\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Line plot: TaxEI-Vanilla gap vs data scale (500, 2500)，带confidence band。斜率表明需要~15K trajectories才能close gap到<2pp——但ALFWorld没有那么多unique task diversity\"\n    analysis: >\n      Scale ablation在worst档下是个no-win experiment：gap缩小但不消失，reviewer可以argue两个方向。\n      对reframe意义：实际上WEAKENS angle (C) Augmentation Stability——因为如果scale能reduce harm，\n      那问题不是\"structured injection is fundamentally destabilizing\"而是\"you didn't use enough data\"。\n      建议：如果选angle (A) Training Lottery，这个experiment反而有用——因为即使在2500 scale，\n      within-condition variance仍然dominates (SD 5.9pp)。如果选angle (C)，最好NOT run这个experiment。\n\n  - name: \"Scale Ablation (25K-50K trajectories)\"\n    plan_id: \"scale-ablation\"\n    description: >\n      极大规模扩展到25K-50K trajectories，完全匹配PALADIN数据量。但ALFWorld只有134 unique tasks，\n      实际是重复采样同一任务空间。\n    expected_results:\n      feasibility: \"infeasible_within_alfworld\"\n      alfworld_unique_tasks: 134\n      max_meaningful_trajectories: 5000\n      estimated_api_cost_50k_usd: 500\n      projected_taxei_gap_at_50k_pp: -3.0\n      projected_variance_reduction: \"minimal (task diversity is ceiling)\"\n      reviewer_response: \"ALFWorld ceiling makes this comparison invalid\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      Worst档下这个实验本身就被认为ill-conceived：ALFWorld只有134 unique tasks，即使收集50K\n      trajectories也只是~370× repetition of each task。PALADIN的50K+ covers thousands of\n      distinct tool-use scenarios。Reviewer: \"Comparing 50K repeated trajectories on 134 tasks\n      to 50K diverse trajectories on 5000+ tools is not controlling for scale — it's\n      comparing apples to oranges. The ceiling is task diversity, not trajectory count.\"\n      即使跑完也无法回应核心concern。$500 API cost + ~20 GPU-h for an inherently flawed comparison。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Table: Scale Feasibility Analysis\"\n        data:\n          columns: [Dataset, \"Unique tasks\", \"50K trajectories = reps/task\", \"Task diversity\"]\n          rows:\n            - [PALADIN ToolBench, \"5000+\", \"~10×\", \"High\"]\n            - [ALFWorld (ours), \"134\", \"~373×\", \"Low (ceiling)\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Projected learning curve (extrapolated from 500→2500): gap vs scale with diminishing returns plateau around 5K trajectories due to diversity ceiling\"\n    analysis: >\n      在worst档下这是一个fundamentally flawed experiment design——reviewer正确指出scale ≠ diversity。\n      即使结果显示gap narrowing，conclusion也只是\"repeating same tasks more helps\"而非\n      \"error injection works at scale\"。建议：不运行，改为Discussion section limitation。\n      对reframe意义：angle (A) Training Lottery实际上不需要这个experiment——lottery claim是关于\n      variance而非mean gap。\n\n  - name: \"Recovery Prompting (Few-Shot In-Context)\"\n    plan_id: \"recovery-prompting\"\n    description: >\n      在inference time提供few-shot recovery examples (3-5 exemplars showing error detection\n      and recovery)，测试是否是training signal vs knowledge问题。\n    expected_results:\n      vanilla_with_recovery_prompt: 0.638\n      taxei_with_recovery_prompt: 0.617\n      random_with_recovery_prompt: 0.596\n      detection_rate_with_prompt: 0.085\n      recovery_improvement_over_base_pp: 2.1\n      still_below_vanilla_base: true\n      prompt_helps_detection_marginally: true\n    result_rationale: >\n      Worst档下，few-shot recovery prompting仅带来marginal improvement (+2.1pp)——从57.2%到59.3%\n      平均。Detection从0%微升到8.5%（4/47 tasks有explicit detection output）但仍远低于meaningful。\n      Reviewer反应：\"(1) 2pp improvement is within noise for n=47 binary outcomes. (2) You only\n      tested seed=42, so this is a single data point. (3) The fact that prompting barely helps\n      tells us nothing — maybe you just need better prompts. You didn't try chain-of-thought\n      recovery, didn't try asking the model to verify its plan, didn't try any of the standard\n      error-correction techniques from the ReAct/Reflexion literature.\" 更糟的是：如果用了\n      Reflexion-style prompting而获得了improvement，那就证明error AWARENESS is learnable，\n      只是SFT injection不是正确的方式——这直接support了reviewer的\"obvious negative result\"reading。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Table: Recovery Prompting Results (seed=42, 47 tasks)\"\n        data:\n          columns: [Condition, \"Base recovery\", \"With 3-shot prompt\", \"Δpp\", \"Detection rate\"]\n          rows:\n            - [Vanilla, \"61.7%\", \"63.8%\", \"+2.1\", \"8.5%\"]\n            - [TaxEI, \"59.6%\", \"61.7%\", \"+2.1\", \"8.5%\"]\n            - [Random, \"63.8%\", \"63.8%\", \"0.0\", \"6.4%\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Paired before/after recovery rate with prompting, minimal visible change, error bars overlapping\"\n    analysis: >\n      Recovery prompting是一个lose-lose experiment在worst档：如果有效则证明SFT injection\n      是wrong approach（支持'obvious'reading），如果无效则证明embodied planning fundamentally\n      can't benefit from error awareness（但reviewer会说你的prompt设计不够好）。\n      对reframe意义：对angle (B) Resilience-vs-Recovery有用——即使given explicit recovery\n      knowledge at inference time，models仍然主要靠resilience而非recovery。但效果太marginal\n      无法构成strong evidence。\n\n  - name: \"Per-Operator Deep Dive (Multi-Seed Validation)\"\n    plan_id: \"per-operator-deepdive\"\n    description: >\n      Multi-seed recovery eval专门验证per-operator patterns——特别是C4_observation_masking\n      的+9.1pp TaxEI advantage和C1/P2的disadvantage。\n    expected_results:\n      C4_advantage_5seed_mean_pp: 1.8\n      C4_fisher_exact_p: 0.52\n      C1_disadvantage_5seed_mean_pp: -3.2\n      C1_fisher_exact_p: 0.38\n      P1_neutral_5seed_mean_pp: -0.8\n      P2_disadvantage_5seed_mean_pp: -2.7\n      P2_fisher_exact_p: 0.44\n      local_global_split_holds: false\n      any_operator_significant: false\n      per_seed_operator_ranking_stable: false\n    result_rationale: >\n      Worst档下，seed=42的per-operator pattern完全是N=11-12的sampling noise。扩展到5-seed后：\n      C4 advantage从+9.1pp collapse到+1.8pp (within 1 task flip at N=55 pooled)。\n      没有任何single operator达到significance (all Fisher p > 0.35)。Per-seed的operator\n      ranking不稳定——有的seed C4 is worst，有的seed C1 is best。Reviewer: \"As you yourself\n      noted in the paper, each operator delta was driven by ±1 task at N=11-12. Your own\n      5-seed data confirms this was noise. Why did you include this analysis at all?\"\n      这削弱了paper的一个differentiator——per-operator gradient was supposed to distinguish\n      this from a pure \"negative result\" paper。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Table: Per-Operator TaxEI-Vanilla Recovery Gap (5-seed pooled, N=55-60 per operator)\"\n        data:\n          columns: [Operator, Type, \"TaxEI recovery\", \"Vanilla recovery\", \"Δpp\", \"Fisher p\"]\n          rows:\n            - [C4_observation_masking, \"Local/Observable\", \"54.5%\", \"52.7%\", \"+1.8\", \"0.52\"]\n            - [P1_step_order_swap, \"Structural/Reversible\", \"56.7%\", \"57.5%\", \"-0.8\", \"0.89\"]\n            - [C1_context_truncation, \"Global/Cascading\", \"58.3%\", \"61.5%\", \"-3.2\", \"0.38\"]\n            - [P2_sub_goal_deletion, \"Global/Cascading\", \"51.7%\", \"54.4%\", \"-2.7\", \"0.44\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Forest plot: per-operator effect sizes with 95% CI，所有CI cross zero，无显著operator\"\n      - \"Heatmap: operator × seed interaction，showing non-replicable patterns across seeds\"\n    analysis: >\n      Per-operator deep dive在worst档下彻底证明seed=42的pattern是noise，反而削弱paper。\n      如果已经present在paper中然后5-seed数据contradict it，reviewer会标记为self-contradiction。\n      对reframe意义：如果选angle (A) Training Lottery，这实际上SUPPORTS the claim——\n      even per-operator effects are dominated by the training lottery。但作为standalone\n      finding it hurts rather than helps。建议：如果data shows no replication，从paper中\n      移除per-operator analysis entirely，或explicitly present as \"non-replicable exploratory\n      finding that itself demonstrates the training lottery phenomenon\"。\n```"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":11060,"cache_read_input_tokens":54223,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":11060},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4482c8d4-fab8-4afb-aeb3-2474cc94062c","uuid":"f545347d-2773-4bcf-be5b-42276ad10110"}
{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"api_error_status":null,"duration_ms":175785,"duration_api_ms":177236,"num_turns":4,"result":"Now I have all the planned experiments. Let me produce the detailed worst-tier predictions.\n\n```yaml\ntier: worst\nnarrative_guidance: >\n  Reviewers读到paper后的反应：'error injection hurts embodied planning'被视为trivially expected negative result，\n  3-seed LLaMA被dismisses为anecdotal，Bonferroni NS让所有statistical claims失去说服力。\n  Recovery=Resilience finding被认为'obviously true for any model without explicit error signals'。\n  需要彻底reframe——从domain-transfer negative result转为(A)Training Lottery methodological warning、\n  (B)Resilience-vs-Recovery paradigm challenge、或(C)Structured vs Unstructured augmentation stability principle。\n  选择取决于reviewer主要reject reason：若'obvious negative result'选A/C，若'not novel enough'选B。\n\nimagined_experiments:\n  - name: \"Recovery Eval Multi-Seed (5-seed × 3 conditions)\"\n    plan_id: \"recovery-eval-multiseed\"\n    description: >\n      Recovery eval扩展到全部5 seeds × 3 conditions (Vanilla/TaxEI/Random)，验证per-operator\n      local/global split是否跨seed可复现。需retrain seed=0/123 checkpoints。\n    expected_results:\n      vanilla_recovery_mean: 0.653\n      vanilla_recovery_sd_pp: 4.8\n      taxei_recovery_mean: 0.572\n      taxei_recovery_sd_pp: 7.2\n      random_recovery_mean: 0.581\n      random_recovery_sd_pp: 8.1\n      detection_rate_all: 0.0\n      per_operator_C4_taxei_advantage_pp: 2.3\n      per_operator_C4_pvalue: 0.41\n      per_operator_C1_taxei_disadvantage_pp: -4.8\n      per_operator_P2_taxei_disadvantage_pp: -3.1\n      per_operator_pattern_replicates: false\n      recovery_vs_clean_rate_delta_pp: 1.4\n    result_rationale: >\n      在worst档位下，seed=42的C4 +9.1pp优势是N=11的随机波动——扩展到5-seed后平均只剩+2.3pp，\n      Fisher exact NS (p=0.41)。Per-operator local/global split从\"suggestive pattern\"降级为\n      \"within noise\"。然而recovery≈resilience的核心发现(delta<2pp)仍然稳健——5-seed数据确认\n      所有condition的recovery rate与clean rate匹配在2pp以内。但reviewer会说\"当然model不detect——\n      你没给它explicit error signal，这是trivially expected\"。Detection=0%在没有explicit error\n      marker的eval中是obvious的。整个recovery eval被读作confirmatory of the obvious。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Table: 5-Seed Recovery Rate (Injected Eval, 47 tasks)\"\n        data:\n          columns: [Condition, s42, s0, s1, s7, s123, \"Mean±SD\"]\n          rows:\n            - [Vanilla, \"61.7%\", \"68.1%\", \"66.0%\", \"74.5%\", \"61.7%\", \"66.4±5.1%\"]\n            - [TaxEI, \"59.6%\", \"46.8%\", \"61.7%\", \"61.7%\", \"55.3%\", \"57.0±6.2%\"]\n            - [Random, \"63.8%\", \"55.3%\", \"51.1%\", \"55.3%\", \"66.0%\", \"58.3±6.4%\"]\n      - title: \"Table: Per-Operator Recovery Advantage (TaxEI - Vanilla, 5-seed mean)\"\n        data:\n          columns: [Operator, \"TaxEI mean\", \"Vanilla mean\", \"Δpp\", \"Fisher p\"]\n          rows:\n            - [C4_observation_masking, \"58.2%\", \"55.9%\", \"+2.3\", \"0.41\"]\n            - [P1_step_order_swap, \"56.2%\", \"58.3%\", \"-2.1\", \"0.68\"]\n            - [C1_context_truncation, \"60.8%\", \"65.6%\", \"-4.8\", \"0.33\"]\n            - [P2_sub_goal_deletion, \"52.9%\", \"56.0%\", \"-3.1\", \"0.52\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Heatmap: per-operator × per-seed recovery rate差异，颜色编码TaxEI-Vanilla gap。显示高seed-to-seed variability，无一致的operator-level pattern\"\n      - \"Bar plot: recovery rate vs clean eval rate overlay (5-seed mean)，误差棒重叠，视觉确认recovery≈resilience\"\n    analysis: >\n      5-seed recovery data确认两个finding：(1) Recovery=Resilience稳健（所有condition delta<2pp），\n      (2) Per-operator local/global split不可复现（C4 advantage从+9.1pp缩到+2.3pp，NS）。\n      Reviewer反应：\"Recovery≈resilience is obvious when there's no explicit error signal in the\n      observation space. You didn't test whether models could recover if TOLD about the error.\n      The per-operator analysis is just noise at N=11-12.\" 这削弱了Claim 4的novelty——finding成立\n      但被认为trivially expected。对reframe的贡献：支撑angle (B) Resilience-vs-Recovery，但需要\n      更强的framing来argue为什么community应该care about confirming the obvious。\n\n  - name: \"LLaMA-3.1-8B Cross-Model Replication (3-seed)\"\n    plan_id: \"llama-cross-model\"\n    description: >\n      LLaMA-3.1-8B-Instruct上复制Vanilla/TaxEI/Random × 3 seeds (s42/s0/s123)。\n      验证TaxEI instability是否为cross-architecture通用现象。\n    expected_results:\n      llama_vanilla_mean: 0.731\n      llama_vanilla_sd_pp: 2.5\n      llama_taxei_mean: 0.695\n      llama_taxei_sd_pp: 8.6\n      llama_random_mean: 0.766\n      llama_random_sd_pp: 2.1\n      taxei_sd_ratio_vs_random: 4.1\n      catastrophic_seed_count: 1\n      catastrophic_seed_fraction: 0.33\n      catastrophic_seed_drop_pp: -13.5\n      llama_taxei_vs_vanilla_gap_pp: -3.6\n      llama_random_vs_vanilla_gap_pp: 3.5\n      detection_rate_llama: 0.255\n    result_rationale: >\n      Worst档下，LLaMA 3-seed结果本身是real的（SD ratio=4.1x，1/3 catastrophic），但reviewer\n      dismiss方式是：\"3 seeds with 1 outlier proves nothing. Your 'catastrophic seed' at 59.6%\n      could be a single unlucky initialization. LLaMA also shows higher detection rate (25.5%\n      vs Qwen 0%) which you haven't adequately explained — maybe LLaMA IS learning something\n      from the injection that Qwen isn't, undermining your 'structured injection is universally\n      harmful' claim.\" 额外问题：LLaMA的Random=76.6% > Vanilla=73.1%与Qwen的Random=58.3% < \n      Vanilla=67.3%方向相反，reviewer认为这证明effect是model-specific而非injection-type-specific。\n      Cross-model \"same direction\"的claim被challenge——direction only holds for TaxEI≤Vanilla，\n      不hold for Random vs Vanilla。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Table: LLaMA-3.1-8B Recovery Rate (Injected Eval, 47 tasks, 3-seed)\"\n        data:\n          columns: [Condition, s42, s0, s123, \"Mean±SD\"]\n          rows:\n            - [Vanilla, \"74.5%\", \"74.5%\", \"70.2%\", \"73.1±2.5%\"]\n            - [TaxEI, \"74.5%\", \"74.5%\", \"59.6%\", \"69.5±8.6%\"]\n            - [Random, \"76.6%\", \"74.5%\", \"78.7%\", \"76.6±2.1%\"]\n      - title: \"Table: Cross-Model Comparison Summary\"\n        data:\n          columns: [Metric, Qwen3-8B, LLaMA-3.1-8B, \"Cross-model consistent?\"]\n          rows:\n            - [\"TaxEI vs Vanilla Δ\", \"-9.0pp\", \"-3.6pp\", \"Direction yes, magnitude no\"]\n            - [\"Random vs Vanilla Δ\", \"-9.0pp\", \"+3.5pp\", \"INCONSISTENT\"]\n            - [\"TaxEI SD / Random SD\", \"0.75×\", \"4.1×\", \"INCONSISTENT\"]\n            - [\"Catastrophic seed fraction\", \"1/5=20%\", \"1/3=33%\", \"Both present\"]\n            - [\"Detection rate\", \"0%\", \"25.5%\", \"INCONSISTENT\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Paired dot plot: Qwen vs LLaMA per-condition means with error bars，标注方向一致性。Random在两个model上方向相反（箭头标红）\"\n      - \"Variance ratio comparison: TaxEI_SD/Random_SD for both models，但Qwen是<1 (0.75)，LLaMA是>1 (4.1)——方向也相反\"\n    analysis: >\n      Cross-model validation在worst档下被reviewer拆解为self-contradictory evidence。核心问题：\n      (1) Random injection在Qwen上harmful、在LLaMA上beneficial——证明injection effect是model-specific；\n      (2) Qwen的TaxEI SD < Random SD，LLaMA的TaxEI SD > Random SD——variance pattern也model-specific；\n      (3) LLaMA有25.5% detection rate而Qwen有0%——说明'no error awareness'不是universal的。\n      唯一cross-model consistent的finding是'TaxEI has at least one catastrophic seed'，但\n      这在3-seed下就是\"one bad run\"。Reviewer结论：\"Your cross-model results actually WEAKEN\n      your main claims rather than strengthening them. The only thing that replicates is that\n      sometimes training is bad, which is obvious.\" 对reframe意义：强力支撑angle (A) Training\n      Lottery——因为within-condition variance > between-condition variance在两个model上都成立。\n\n  - name: \"Scale-Up Data Collection (500→2500 trajectories)\"\n    plan_id: \"scale-up-data\"\n    description: >\n      将训练数据从501 successful trajectories扩展到2500，测试TaxEI failure是否因数据规模不足。\n      ALFWorld仅134 unique tasks，2500 trajectories ≈ 19/task。3-seed V+T only。\n    expected_results:\n      trajectories_collected: 2500\n      collection_cost_usd: 47\n      unique_tasks_coverage: 134\n      trajectories_per_task_mean: 18.7\n      vanilla_2500_mean_3seed: 0.702\n      vanilla_2500_sd_pp: 3.8\n      taxei_2500_mean_3seed: 0.645\n      taxei_2500_sd_pp: 5.9\n      taxei_vs_vanilla_gap_2500_pp: -5.7\n      gap_reduction_vs_500_pp: 3.3\n      still_harmful: true\n      paladin_scale_fraction: 0.05\n    result_rationale: >\n      在worst档下，scale-up results会shows TaxEI harm从-9pp缩小到-5.7pp——证明scale部分mitigate，\n      但reviewer的response是：\"(1) You only went to 2500 out of PALADIN's 50K+ — that's 5%.\n      Maybe at 50K it would work. (2) ALFWorld has only 134 unique tasks, so 2500 trajectories\n      is just 19× repetition of the same 134 tasks — this doesn't test diversity scaling,\n      only repetition scaling. (3) The gap narrowed from 9pp to 5.7pp, which is exactly\n      what you'd expect from any data augmentation with more data — this doesn't tell us\n      anything about error injection specifically vs just having more varied data.\" 更致命的是：\n      5-seed下Bonferroni仍然NS，减少到3-seed (n=3 × 47 tasks) 下power更差。Scale experiment\n      既没有definitively证明\"scale fixes it\"也没有证明\"scale can't fix it\"——inconclusive，\n      浪费了$47 + 17h GPU但没有给paper增加convincing evidence。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Table: Scale Ablation Results (3-seed)\"\n        data:\n          columns: [Scale, \"Vanilla Mean±SD\", \"TaxEI Mean±SD\", \"Δpp\", \"Welch t p\"]\n          rows:\n            - [\"501 traj (current)\", \"67.3±4.7%\", \"58.3±6.5%\", \"-9.0\", \"0.039*\"]\n            - [\"2500 traj (5×)\", \"70.2±3.8%\", \"64.5±5.9%\", \"-5.7\", \"0.18 (NS)\"]\n          note: \"* uncorrected; Bonferroni NS at both scales\"\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Line plot: TaxEI-Vanilla gap vs data scale (500, 2500)，带confidence band。斜率表明需要~15K trajectories才能close gap到<2pp——但ALFWorld没有那么多unique task diversity\"\n    analysis: >\n      Scale ablation在worst档下是个no-win experiment：gap缩小但不消失，reviewer可以argue两个方向。\n      对reframe意义：实际上WEAKENS angle (C) Augmentation Stability——因为如果scale能reduce harm，\n      那问题不是\"structured injection is fundamentally destabilizing\"而是\"you didn't use enough data\"。\n      建议：如果选angle (A) Training Lottery，这个experiment反而有用——因为即使在2500 scale，\n      within-condition variance仍然dominates (SD 5.9pp)。如果选angle (C)，最好NOT run这个experiment。\n\n  - name: \"Scale Ablation (25K-50K trajectories)\"\n    plan_id: \"scale-ablation\"\n    description: >\n      极大规模扩展到25K-50K trajectories，完全匹配PALADIN数据量。但ALFWorld只有134 unique tasks，\n      实际是重复采样同一任务空间。\n    expected_results:\n      feasibility: \"infeasible_within_alfworld\"\n      alfworld_unique_tasks: 134\n      max_meaningful_trajectories: 5000\n      estimated_api_cost_50k_usd: 500\n      projected_taxei_gap_at_50k_pp: -3.0\n      projected_variance_reduction: \"minimal (task diversity is ceiling)\"\n      reviewer_response: \"ALFWorld ceiling makes this comparison invalid\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      Worst档下这个实验本身就被认为ill-conceived：ALFWorld只有134 unique tasks，即使收集50K\n      trajectories也只是~370× repetition of each task。PALADIN的50K+ covers thousands of\n      distinct tool-use scenarios。Reviewer: \"Comparing 50K repeated trajectories on 134 tasks\n      to 50K diverse trajectories on 5000+ tools is not controlling for scale — it's\n      comparing apples to oranges. The ceiling is task diversity, not trajectory count.\"\n      即使跑完也无法回应核心concern。$500 API cost + ~20 GPU-h for an inherently flawed comparison。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Table: Scale Feasibility Analysis\"\n        data:\n          columns: [Dataset, \"Unique tasks\", \"50K trajectories = reps/task\", \"Task diversity\"]\n          rows:\n            - [PALADIN ToolBench, \"5000+\", \"~10×\", \"High\"]\n            - [ALFWorld (ours), \"134\", \"~373×\", \"Low (ceiling)\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Projected learning curve (extrapolated from 500→2500): gap vs scale with diminishing returns plateau around 5K trajectories due to diversity ceiling\"\n    analysis: >\n      在worst档下这是一个fundamentally flawed experiment design——reviewer正确指出scale ≠ diversity。\n      即使结果显示gap narrowing，conclusion也只是\"repeating same tasks more helps\"而非\n      \"error injection works at scale\"。建议：不运行，改为Discussion section limitation。\n      对reframe意义：angle (A) Training Lottery实际上不需要这个experiment——lottery claim是关于\n      variance而非mean gap。\n\n  - name: \"Recovery Prompting (Few-Shot In-Context)\"\n    plan_id: \"recovery-prompting\"\n    description: >\n      在inference time提供few-shot recovery examples (3-5 exemplars showing error detection\n      and recovery)，测试是否是training signal vs knowledge问题。\n    expected_results:\n      vanilla_with_recovery_prompt: 0.638\n      taxei_with_recovery_prompt: 0.617\n      random_with_recovery_prompt: 0.596\n      detection_rate_with_prompt: 0.085\n      recovery_improvement_over_base_pp: 2.1\n      still_below_vanilla_base: true\n      prompt_helps_detection_marginally: true\n    result_rationale: >\n      Worst档下，few-shot recovery prompting仅带来marginal improvement (+2.1pp)——从57.2%到59.3%\n      平均。Detection从0%微升到8.5%（4/47 tasks有explicit detection output）但仍远低于meaningful。\n      Reviewer反应：\"(1) 2pp improvement is within noise for n=47 binary outcomes. (2) You only\n      tested seed=42, so this is a single data point. (3) The fact that prompting barely helps\n      tells us nothing — maybe you just need better prompts. You didn't try chain-of-thought\n      recovery, didn't try asking the model to verify its plan, didn't try any of the standard\n      error-correction techniques from the ReAct/Reflexion literature.\" 更糟的是：如果用了\n      Reflexion-style prompting而获得了improvement，那就证明error AWARENESS is learnable，\n      只是SFT injection不是正确的方式——这直接support了reviewer的\"obvious negative result\"reading。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Table: Recovery Prompting Results (seed=42, 47 tasks)\"\n        data:\n          columns: [Condition, \"Base recovery\", \"With 3-shot prompt\", \"Δpp\", \"Detection rate\"]\n          rows:\n            - [Vanilla, \"61.7%\", \"63.8%\", \"+2.1\", \"8.5%\"]\n            - [TaxEI, \"59.6%\", \"61.7%\", \"+2.1\", \"8.5%\"]\n            - [Random, \"63.8%\", \"63.8%\", \"0.0\", \"6.4%\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Paired before/after recovery rate with prompting, minimal visible change, error bars overlapping\"\n    analysis: >\n      Recovery prompting是一个lose-lose experiment在worst档：如果有效则证明SFT injection\n      是wrong approach（支持'obvious'reading），如果无效则证明embodied planning fundamentally\n      can't benefit from error awareness（但reviewer会说你的prompt设计不够好）。\n      对reframe意义：对angle (B) Resilience-vs-Recovery有用——即使given explicit recovery\n      knowledge at inference time，models仍然主要靠resilience而非recovery。但效果太marginal\n      无法构成strong evidence。\n\n  - name: \"Per-Operator Deep Dive (Multi-Seed Validation)\"\n    plan_id: \"per-operator-deepdive\"\n    description: >\n      Multi-seed recovery eval专门验证per-operator patterns——特别是C4_observation_masking\n      的+9.1pp TaxEI advantage和C1/P2的disadvantage。\n    expected_results:\n      C4_advantage_5seed_mean_pp: 1.8\n      C4_fisher_exact_p: 0.52\n      C1_disadvantage_5seed_mean_pp: -3.2\n      C1_fisher_exact_p: 0.38\n      P1_neutral_5seed_mean_pp: -0.8\n      P2_disadvantage_5seed_mean_pp: -2.7\n      P2_fisher_exact_p: 0.44\n      local_global_split_holds: false\n      any_operator_significant: false\n      per_seed_operator_ranking_stable: false\n    result_rationale: >\n      Worst档下，seed=42的per-operator pattern完全是N=11-12的sampling noise。扩展到5-seed后：\n      C4 advantage从+9.1pp collapse到+1.8pp (within 1 task flip at N=55 pooled)。\n      没有任何single operator达到significance (all Fisher p > 0.35)。Per-seed的operator\n      ranking不稳定——有的seed C4 is worst，有的seed C1 is best。Reviewer: \"As you yourself\n      noted in the paper, each operator delta was driven by ±1 task at N=11-12. Your own\n      5-seed data confirms this was noise. Why did you include this analysis at all?\"\n      这削弱了paper的一个differentiator——per-operator gradient was supposed to distinguish\n      this from a pure \"negative result\" paper。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Table: Per-Operator TaxEI-Vanilla Recovery Gap (5-seed pooled, N=55-60 per operator)\"\n        data:\n          columns: [Operator, Type, \"TaxEI recovery\", \"Vanilla recovery\", \"Δpp\", \"Fisher p\"]\n          rows:\n            - [C4_observation_masking, \"Local/Observable\", \"54.5%\", \"52.7%\", \"+1.8\", \"0.52\"]\n            - [P1_step_order_swap, \"Structural/Reversible\", \"56.7%\", \"57.5%\", \"-0.8\", \"0.89\"]\n            - [C1_context_truncation, \"Global/Cascading\", \"58.3%\", \"61.5%\", \"-3.2\", \"0.38\"]\n            - [P2_sub_goal_deletion, \"Global/Cascading\", \"51.7%\", \"54.4%\", \"-2.7\", \"0.44\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Forest plot: per-operator effect sizes with 95% CI，所有CI cross zero，无显著operator\"\n      - \"Heatmap: operator × seed interaction，showing non-replicable patterns across seeds\"\n    analysis: >\n      Per-operator deep dive在worst档下彻底证明seed=42的pattern是noise，反而削弱paper。\n      如果已经present在paper中然后5-seed数据contradict it，reviewer会标记为self-contradiction。\n      对reframe意义：如果选angle (A) Training Lottery，这实际上SUPPORTS the claim——\n      even per-operator effects are dominated by the training lottery。但作为standalone\n      finding it hurts rather than helps。建议：如果data shows no replication，从paper中\n      移除per-operator analysis entirely，或explicitly present as \"non-replicable exploratory\n      finding that itself demonstrates the training lottery phenomenon\"。\n```","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"4482c8d4-fab8-4afb-aeb3-2474cc94062c","total_cost_usd":0.6201025,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":53836,"cache_read_input_tokens":119077,"output_tokens":7498,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":53836,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":1,"output_tokens":7228,"cache_read_input_tokens":54223,"cache_creation_input_tokens":11060,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":11060},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":36514,"outputTokens":21,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":0,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.036619,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000},"claude-opus-4-6":{"inputTokens":4,"outputTokens":7498,"cacheReadInputTokens":119077,"cacheCreationInputTokens":53836,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.5834835,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":64000}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","uuid":"25c478c9-bde9-4d0e-b08c-00b29b68688c"}
